Browser evaluation of the page served from this repository on 4879, opened with the printed link.
Chrome on macOS, dark scheme, through the Claude in Chrome extension, on the real machine (four
repositories, five sessions; other repositories' names are left out). Values are from the live DOM,
with popups opened by dispatching the same mouseover and focus events a person causes, and one
screenshot. Observed at the working tree that became 3562625 (the commit popup and the board
header's popup were added during this pass and re-observed).

EVAL-001 references are links
  Repositories: every repository name, every change under it, every phase next to a change, and every
    command's change and phase are links.
  Board: every column header (00 intake ... 15 learn) links to that phase in the Workflow (32 links
    across the two tables); every flag that points somewhere is a link: "3 advisories" to the change,
    "Session open: claude" to Running, "Interrupted: <phase>" to that gate, "Failing" and "Stale
    evidence" to the first such gate.
  A change: the advisory "independent review (13-review)" links 13-review; the check detail
    "predecessor complete: 13-review" links it; the gate panel's skill carries "what this phase is
    for" linking the Workflow; every timeline event's phase is a link (6 on this change); the spend
    table's phases are links; "Rerun from verification" links the verify gate; a running command's
    phase and an interrupted run's phase are links; the session note links to Running.
  Workflow: "Then judge", every "Can return to" target, both ends of each way back (10 links), and
    each track's required and not-required phases (5 links) are links.
  Running: each session's repository and change are links; a running command's phase is a link
    when there is one (none was running at the time).

EVAL-002 the popup says what a reference points at, and where it lives
  Hovering a repository card's name: "soft_foundry / 1 session open, 7 open changes, 18 closed. /
    ~/dev/soft_foundry/ (.ai/workflow.yml, changes/)".
  Hovering a change: "ui-explainer-timeline in soft_foundry / <title>. in progress, phase learn. /
    changes/ui-explainer-timeline/metadata.yml".
  Hovering a gate reference inside the change: "13-review: Pass / Handoff complete. 9 checks, none
    failing. / changes/ui-explainer-timeline/13-review/handoff.yml" (screenshot: a dark box under the
    link with the title, the sentence, and the path in monospace beneath a rule).
  Hovering a phase reference: "15 learn / Worked by the learning skill into 15-learning/. Its gate
    runs 10 checks; it must produce findings.md, proposed-rules.md, proposed-evals.md, instincts.yml,
    handoff.yml. / .ai/workflow.yml, .ai/skills/learning/".
  Hovering a commit: "Commit ab1723b2ace5 / The commit this phase's evidence describes. See it with
    git show ab1723b2ace5. / .git (git show ab1723b2ace5)".
  Hovering a change in another repository, from Running: its slug and repository, status and phase,
    and the path with that repository's directory in front:
    "~/.../<repo>/changes/<slug>/metadata.yml".
  Hovering a repository from Running: its sessions, open and closed counts, and its path.

EVAL-003 the popup is a tooltip
  Focusing a gate link with the keyboard opens the same popup; the link gets aria-describedby="tip";
    the popup element has role="tooltip". Escape closes it. Moving focus away closes it. Navigating
    closes it.
  No sideways page scroll on any page at the window's width.

Not exercised: a screen reader (whether the described-by text is read with the link); the light
scheme; 200% zoom; pointer hover of the popup itself to keep it open (the code keeps it open while
the pointer is over it; this was not driven).
